<title>USA: U.S. soymeal weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soymeal weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA soymeal export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 119,300 MT were 2.3 times the previous week and one-third above the four-week average.  Major increases for Turkey (51,200 MT), Denmark (37,500 MT), Spain (27,500 MT), Japan (20,600 MT), and Saudi Arabia (20,000 MT) were partially offset by reductions for unknown destinations (72,000 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 306,400 MT -- a marketing-year high -- were three percent above the previous week and three-quarters more than four-week average.  The Philippines (55,500 MT), China (52,500 MT), Spain (38,500 MT), and Denmark (37,500 MT) were the major recipients.</p>
</text>
